      "category": "igaming",
      "title": "iGaming Shake-Up: What African Bettors Need to Know",
      "slug": "igaming-shake-up-african-bettors",
      "excerpt": "From Romania's ONJN leadership change to South Africa's NGB blocking plan, here\u2019s how recent iGaming news impacts African bettors and their deposits.",
      "body": "# iGaming Shake-Up: What African Bettors Need to Know  \n\nEish, the iGaming world is buzzing with fresh developments, and African bettors need to stay sharp! From regulatory shifts in Europe to revenue surges in the US, these changes could ripple all the way to your deposits and betting options. Let\u2019s break down the latest news and what it means for punters across Nigeria, Kenya, South Africa, Ghana, and Tanzania.  \n\n## ONJN Leadership Change in Romania: Why It Matters  \nAccording to **SBC News**, Vlad-Cristian Soare has been abruptly dismissed as President of Romania\u2019s Gambling Office (ONJN). This might seem like a distant European story, but here\u2019s the kicker: Many African-facing betting platforms operate under licenses from jurisdictions like Romania. A leadership shake-up could mean stricter regulations or licensing changes, potentially affecting the availability of certain bookmakers in Africa.  \n\nFor bettors using platforms licensed in Romania, this is the kind of news that could impact your options down the line. Keep an eye on updates from your favorite sites\u2014whether it\u2019s **Bet9ja**, **1xBet**, or **Melbet**\u2014to ensure they\u2019re staying compliant.  \n\n## South Africa\u2019s NGB Cracks Down on Illegal Sites  \nCloser to home, **iGaming Business** reports that South Africa\u2019s National Gambling Board (NGB) is advancing its plan to block illegal online gambling websites. With the deadline for Expressions of Interest (EOI) approaching, this move could reshape the country\u2019s iGaming landscape.  \n\nFor South African bettors, this means a safer betting environment but also potentially fewer options if your go-to site ends up on the chopping block. If you\u2019re using **Hollywoodbets** or **Betway**, you\u2019re likely in the clear, but smaller, unlicensed platforms might face the axe.  \n\n## Connecticut\u2019s iGaming Boom: Lessons for Africa  \nOver in the US, **Iredell Free News** highlights Connecticut\u2019s combined betting and iGaming revenue climbing to a whopping $2.05 billion in July\u2014a 13% increase. This growth underscores the potential of regulated iGaming markets, a lesson African regulators could take to heart.  \n\nFor African bettors, this is a reminder of the importance of choosing licensed platforms. As markets like Nigeria, Kenya, and Ghana mature, we could see similar revenue surges, but only if regulators and operators play their cards right.  \n\n## Digitain Expands in the UK: What\u2019s in It for Africa?  \n**SBC News** also reports that Digitain, a leading technology provider, has expanded its UK presence through a partnership with Silkbet. While this is a UK-focused move, Digitain\u2019s technology powers many African betting platforms, including **Sportybet** and **Betika**.  \n\nThis expansion could mean better odds, smoother interfaces, and more innovative features for African bettors. If you\u2019re a tech-savvy punter, this is good news\u2014compare the latest offerings on **SifuFinds** to see which platforms are leveraging Digitain\u2019s upgrades.  \n\n## The Black Market Threat: A Global Concern  \nThe **Betting and Gaming Council (BGC)** warns that the UK\u2019s black market could take \u00a31 billion in Premier League bets next season, as reported by **SBC News**. This isn\u2019t just a UK problem\u2014pirate streaming and illegal betting sites are a growing concern across Africa too.  \n\nFor African bettors, this is a reminder to stick with trusted, licensed platforms. While the odds on **BetKing** or **Betway** might not always be as flashy as those on shady sites, they come with the peace of mind that your deposits are safe.  \n\n## Evolution\u2019s Takeover Drama: What\u2019s at Stake?  \nIn corporate news, **iGaming Business** reports that Evolution\u2019s board has recommended shareholders reject Candle Lake Limited\u2019s mandatory takeover offer. This high-stakes drama could impact the live casino games you enjoy on platforms like **1xBet** and **Bet9ja**.  \n\nWhile the outcome is still uncertain, this is the kind of news that could shake up the live gaming market. If you\u2019re a fan of Evolution\u2019s games, keep an eye on how this story unfolds\u2014it could affect game availability and quality.  \n\n## 888AFRICA Ups Its Game: Competition Heats Up  \nFinally, **SBC News** highlights that 888AFRICA is boosting its marketing capabilities as competition in the African market grows. With major international players eyeing the continent, this means better promotions, bonuses, and user experiences for bettors.  \n\nIf you\u2019re in Nigeria, Kenya, or Ghana, this is your cue to compare offers across **Bet9ja**, **Sportybet**, and **888AFRICA**. The more competition, the better the deals for you\u2014check out **SifuFinds** to stay on top of the latest promotions.  \n\n## Responsible Gambling: A Quick Reminder  \nWith all this iGaming news, it\u2019s easy to get caught up in the excitement. But remember, betting should always be fun and responsible. Set limits, stick to your budget, and never chase losses. If you\u2019re in South Africa, Kenya, or Nigeria, resources like the National Responsible Gambling Programme (NRGP) and Betting Control and Licensing Board (BCLB) are here to help.  \n\n## Final Thoughts  \nFrom Romania to South Africa, these iGaming developments are reshaping the global betting landscape\u2014and African bettors are right in the thick of it. Whether it\u2019s regulatory changes, technological upgrades, or corporate drama, staying informed is your best bet.  \n\nFor the latest odds, promotions, and platform comparisons, head over to **SifuFinds**. We\u2019ve got you covered, no matter where you\u2019re betting from.  \n\n*18+ | Bet Responsibly | T&Cs Apply*",
